ero or less are never taken. Parallel edges are distinct and may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both be taken. Which optimum is returned when several exist is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order and ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per edge in position order.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That of the network simplex on n + 2 vertices and n + m + 1 arcs; polynomial","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in practice, O(n² m) in the worst case of its pivots.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition"},{"type":"text","text":" is this graph’s; every capacity is at least zero and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacities fit in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"; |weight| fits the network simplex’s cost bound (4(n + 3)(the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greatest weight + 1) fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"maximumWeightBMatching(bipartition:capacity:weight:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14MatchingModuleE22maximumWeightBMatching11bipartition8capacity6weightAD0G0Vyxqd__G15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionVyxG_Si6VertexQzXEqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXEtSZRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"MatchingModule"}],"fragment